      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'm seeing a lot of volatility in areas that are undergoing pretty rapid demographic shifts though. some of my managers are worried that when the \"character\" of a neighborhood changes—like when you see certain types of local retail being replaced or the population makeup shifting—it's actually a leading indicator of instability. from a risk analysis standpoint, how much weight should we be putting on those kinds of cultural or demographic changes as a predictor for economic volatility?",
